'' A MODULE'S DECLARATIONS HAVE NO ORDER (ADR 0017; RFC-0003 §5). acme.early uses, above
'' their declarations -- in its own file or in b.bas, which sorts after it -- a procedure,
'' a type by value and as a field, an enum member, a const built from a later const, a
'' typedef chain, a generic and its member body, a generic typedef, a namespace member, a
'' shared variable and a base type, and defines members out of line above their types. The
'' importer reads the module's interface, in the module's order, and takes it too. 1197 is
'' every term right; the second call's shared counter makes it 1198.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target win64-msvc -i tests/modules/src/fwd/libs tests/modules/src/fwd/app/main.bas -o tests/modules/orderlink.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=toolchains/tiko-windows/lib/win64-msvc
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' RUN: tests/modules/orderlink.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  1197
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  1198
